// Detects DNS queries from one source IP address under one parent domain
// (its last two labels) with many different long, random subdomains: the
// pattern of data encoded into DNS names (DNS tunnelling, scenario #4).
//
// The main condition is the number of different subdomains per source and
// parent domain. Length and entropy are secondary: they drop short or
// repetitive names, but a long name made of words scores about as high as a
// random one (3.9 for the AMA endpoints), so they cannot decide on their own.
//
// Exclusions:
// - Microsoft zones (opinsights, storage, core.windows.net, monitor): a tunnel
//   needs the attacker to run the parent domain's authoritative name server,
//   and Microsoft runs these, so they cannot carry one. Their names are random
//   by design (storage accounts, disks, the workspace ID) and would match.
// - .internal.cloudapp.net: the VNet's DNS search suffix. A failed lookup is
//   retried with it appended, but the bare name is logged first, so dropping
//   the suffixed copy loses no query (evidence D1).
//
// Limits:
// - Parent = last two labels: a suffix such as co.uk is split wrongly, and all
//   *.azure.com names from one source are counted together.
// - Entropy is computed over the whole subdomain, dots included.
// - Threshold: on 2026-11-05 the baseline was at most 3 qualifying subdomains
//   per source and parent over 2 hours. A tunnel sending 10 names or fewer
//   an hour is missed.
// - Only queries to Azure DNS are logged. DNS sent straight to an outside
//   server is not in DNSQueryLogs; it crosses the NVA and the flow logs.
DNSQueryLogs
| extend CleanQueryName = trim_end(@"\.+", QueryName)
| where not(
  CleanQueryName endswith ".opinsights.azure.com"
  or CleanQueryName endswith ".storage.azure.net"
  or CleanQueryName endswith ".core.windows.net"
  or CleanQueryName endswith ".monitor.azure.com"
  or CleanQueryName endswith ".internal.cloudapp.net")
| extend Parent = extract(@'([^.]+\.[^.]+)$', 1, CleanQueryName)
| extend Sub = trim_end(@"\.+", substring(CleanQueryName, 0, strlen(CleanQueryName) - strlen(Parent)))
| where strlen(Sub) >= 25
| distinct SourceIpAddress, Parent, Sub
| extend Chars = extract_all(@"(.)", Sub)
| mv-expand Chars to typeof(string)
| summarize N = count() by SourceIpAddress, Parent, Sub, Chars
| extend P = todouble(N) / strlen(Sub)
| summarize Entropy = -sum(P * log2(P)) by SourceIpAddress, Parent, Sub
| where Entropy >= 3.3
| summarize Queries = count(), Distinct = dcount(Sub) by SourceIpAddress, Parent
| where Distinct > 10

